## HTML Delivery Standards

All HTML deliverables must follow these rules for smooth Figma + Webflow compatibility:

### Structure
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>[Project Name] — Built by Kadeio</title>
  <!-- Google Fonts or self-hosted fonts -->
  <style>
    /* All styles inline or in <style> block */
    /* Use CSS custom properties (variables) for all colors, spacing, type */
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <!-- SECTIONS: clearly commented -->
  <!-- NAV -->
  <!-- HERO -->
  <!-- FEATURES / CONTENT -->
  <!-- CTA -->
  <!-- FOOTER -->

  <!-- Built by Kadeio -->
</body>
</html>
```

### CSS Rules
- All colors defined as CSS variables in `:root`
- Use `rem` for typography, `px` for borders/shadows
- No external CSS frameworks (Tailwind, Bootstrap) unless explicitly requested
- Animations via CSS keyframes or Intersection Observer JS

### GitHub-Ready Formatting
- Single-file HTML (all CSS/JS inline) unless project is multi-page
- Clean indentation (2 spaces)
- Semantic HTML5 elements (`<section>`, `<nav>`, `<article>`, `<footer>`)
- Comments label every major section

